                            <comment id="237920" author="jamesanunez" created="Tue, 4 Dec 2018 15:43:01 +0000">&lt;p&gt;I don't see any evidence that the connectathon test was run with a striped directory.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="237881" author="adilger" created="Tue, 4 Dec 2018 01:07:46 +0000">&lt;p&gt;The failing test "telldir cookies" relates to being able to restart "&lt;tt&gt;readdir()&lt;/tt&gt;" operations at a specific spot.  It isn't totally surprising that this would be having problems on a DNE striped directory (if that is what is being tested), since this is one of the more complex parts of DNE to combine.  However, it isn't totally clear to me what the test is trying to do.  The Lustre logs show a lot of seeking around in the directory, and then finally the test fails when it returns to directory offset 0.  There are a large number of connectathon tests passing, so it isn't necessarily a critical/common issue.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
